---
description: Project rules for Opportunity & Deadline Radar
alwaysApply: true
---

- Read docs/SPEC.md before any task; it is the source of truth for schema and behavior.
- Work only on the task in the current prompt. Do not add features, refactor unrelated files, or change the stack.
- Every new module needs pytest tests. Collectors must be tested against saved fixture files in tests/fixtures/, never live network.
- Run `make test` and `make lint` before saying a task is done, and paste the output.
- No secrets in code. Everything via env vars.
- Prefer small pure functions. Type hints everywhere.
- Never guess data. Unknown stays null/unknown. A failing source is an error result, never an empty list.
- If a requirement is ambiguous, ask me instead of guessing.
